The line #NormalTok("set.seed(2026)"); fixes R's random number generator, so that the "random" samples are the same every time the code runs and the results match this book. Any analysis that involves randomness should fix the seed in this way.

The thousand averages form a #strong[sampling distribution]: the distribution of a statistic over many possible samples. #ref(<fig-clt>, supplement: [Figure]) compares the sampling distributions for samples of 5 and of 30 students.

