== One-way ANOVA
<one-way-anova>
The first question is whether stress differs between the five faculties. One approach would be a t-test for every pair of faculties, but that is 10 tests. Chapter 7 showed that each test has a 5% chance of a false alarm, and that the risks accumulate: across 10 independent tests, the chance of at least one false alarm is about 40%. #strong[Analysis of variance] (ANOVA) avoids the problem by asking one question first: whether the faculty averages differ #emph[at all].

=== Partitioning variation
<partitioning-variation>
ANOVA compares two kinds of variation. Stress scores for three small groups show the idea:

#block[
#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("group_scores ");#OtherTok("<-");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("tibble");#NormalTok("(");],
[#NormalTok("  ");#AttributeTok("group  =");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("rep");#NormalTok("(");#FunctionTok("c");#NormalTok("(");#StringTok("\"A\"");#NormalTok(", ");#StringTok("\"B\"");#NormalTok(", ");#StringTok("\"C\"");#NormalTok("), ");#AttributeTok("each =");#NormalTok(" ");#DecValTok("4");#NormalTok("),");],
[#NormalTok("  ");#AttributeTok("stress =");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("c");#NormalTok("(");#FloatTok("2.5");#NormalTok(", ");#FloatTok("3.0");#NormalTok(", ");#FloatTok("2.8");#NormalTok(", ");#FloatTok("3.1");#NormalTok(",   ");#FloatTok("3.4");#NormalTok(", ");#FloatTok("3.8");#NormalTok(", ");#FloatTok("3.5");#NormalTok(", ");#FloatTok("3.9");#NormalTok(",   ");#FloatTok("2.9");#NormalTok(", ");#FloatTok("3.3");#NormalTok(", ");#FloatTok("3.0");#NormalTok(", ");#FloatTok("3.4");#NormalTok(")");],
[#NormalTok(")");],
[#NormalTok("group_scores ");#SpecialCharTok("|>");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("summarise");#NormalTok("(");#AttributeTok("mean =");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("mean");#NormalTok("(stress), ");#AttributeTok(".by =");#NormalTok(" group)");],));
#block[
#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("# A tibble: 3 × 2");],
[#NormalTok("  group  mean");],
[#NormalTok("  <chr> <dbl>");],
[#NormalTok("1 A      2.85");],
[#NormalTok("2 B      3.65");],
[#NormalTok("3 C      3.15");],));
]
]
#ref(<fig-partition>, supplement: [Figure]) draws the twelve scores, the average of each group, and the overall average. The group averages differ from the overall average: that is variation #strong[between] groups. The scores also differ from their own group's average: that is variation #strong[within] groups.

#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("group_means ");#OtherTok("<-");#NormalTok(" group_scores ");#SpecialCharTok("|>");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("summarise");#NormalTok("(");#AttributeTok("mean =");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("mean");#NormalTok("(stress), ");#AttributeTok(".by =");#NormalTok(" group)");],
