R's #NormalTok("trees"); dataset records the girth, height, and timber volume of 31 felled black cherry trees. Foresters need to estimate a standing tree's volume from measurements they can take without cutting it down, a classic job for multiple regression:

#block[
#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("tree_model ");#OtherTok("<-");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("lm");#NormalTok("(Volume ");#SpecialCharTok("~");#NormalTok(" Girth ");#SpecialCharTok("+");#NormalTok(" Height, ");#AttributeTok("data =");#NormalTok(" trees)");],
