=== Describing the clusters
<describing-the-clusters>
A cluster is only useful if its meaning can be stated. Adding the cluster to the original, unscaled data and averaging each variable by cluster shows each group's profile:

#block[
#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("profiles ");#SpecialCharTok("|>");],
[#NormalTok("  ");#FunctionTok("mutate");#NormalTok("(");#AttributeTok("cluster =");#NormalTok(" clusters");#SpecialCharTok("$");#NormalTok("cluster) ");#SpecialCharTok("|>");],
[#NormalTok("  ");#FunctionTok("summarise");#NormalTok("(");#AttributeTok("students =");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("n");#NormalTok("(), ");#FunctionTok("across");#NormalTok("(sleep_hours");#SpecialCharTok(":");#NormalTok("satisfaction, ");#SpecialCharTok("~");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("round");#NormalTok("(");#FunctionTok("mean");#NormalTok("(.x), ");#DecValTok("1");#NormalTok(")),");],
[#NormalTok("            ");#AttributeTok(".by =");#NormalTok(" cluster) ");#SpecialCharTok("|>");],
[#NormalTok("  ");#FunctionTok("arrange");#NormalTok("(cluster)");],));
#block[
#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("  cluster students sleep_hours study_hours caffeine_mg exercise_days stress");],
[#NormalTok("1       1       85         5.1        41.6       423.7           1.2    3.6");],
[#NormalTok("2       2      197         6.7        18.0       149.8           2.2    3.4");],
[#NormalTok("3       3      200         7.2        23.6       122.9           3.5    2.6");],
[#NormalTok("4       4      117         5.8        40.8       188.1           1.5    3.6");],
