The yardstick package calculates the measures. The function #NormalTok("metric_set()"); bundles several, and because "Yes" is the first level of the outcome, they treat "Yes" as the event of interest:

#block[
#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("class_metrics ");#OtherTok("<-");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("metric_set");#NormalTok("(accuracy, sensitivity, specificity, precision, f_meas)");],
[#NormalTok("test_results ");#SpecialCharTok("|>");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("class_metrics");#NormalTok("(");#AttributeTok("truth =");#NormalTok(" considering_dropout, ");#AttributeTok("estimate =");#NormalTok(" .pred_class)");],));
