=== Costs of the two errors
<costs-of-the-two-errors>
Moving the threshold trades one error for the other, so the choice depends on how much each error costs. The costs are not statistical quantities; they are judgements about consequences, and they should be made explicitly. Suppose the counselling service judges that missing a student who is at risk is ten times as costly as an unnecessary conversation. The total cost of each threshold can then be calculated from the cross-validated predictions:

#block[
#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("cost_miss        ");#OtherTok("<-");#NormalTok(" ");#DecValTok("10");#NormalTok("   ");#CommentTok("# a student at risk who is not contacted");],
[#NormalTok("cost_false_alarm ");#OtherTok("<-");#NormalTok(" ");#DecValTok("1");#NormalTok("    ");#CommentTok("# an unnecessary conversation");],
[],
[#NormalTok("cost_curve ");#OtherTok("<-");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("map");#NormalTok("(");#FunctionTok("seq");#NormalTok("(");#FloatTok("0.02");#NormalTok(", ");#FloatTok("0.6");#NormalTok(", ");#AttributeTok("by =");#NormalTok(" ");#FloatTok("0.02");#NormalTok("), \\(t) {");],
[#NormalTok("  cv_predictions ");#SpecialCharTok("|>");],
[#NormalTok("    ");#FunctionTok("summarise");#NormalTok("(");#AttributeTok("threshold    =");#NormalTok(" t,");],
[#NormalTok("              ");#AttributeTok("misses       =");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("sum");#NormalTok("(.pred_Yes ");#SpecialCharTok("<");#NormalTok(" t ");#SpecialCharTok("&");#NormalTok(" considering_dropout ");#SpecialCharTok("==");#NormalTok(" ");#StringTok("\"Yes\"");#NormalTok("),");],
[#NormalTok("              ");#AttributeTok("false_alarms =");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("sum");#NormalTok("(.pred_Yes ");#SpecialCharTok(">=");#NormalTok(" t ");#SpecialCharTok("&");#NormalTok(" considering_dropout ");#SpecialCharTok("==");#NormalTok(" ");#StringTok("\"No\"");#NormalTok("),");],
