Sensitivity, specificity, precision, and F1 all depend on the threshold, so a paper that reports them must say which threshold was used, and why. The AUC does not depend on the threshold, which is why it is the standard measure for comparing models, and the threshold-dependent measures are the ones for describing how a model will be used.

