The argument #NormalTok("names_glue"); builds the new column names, such as #NormalTok("gpa_s1"); and #NormalTok("sleep_hours_s2");, and #NormalTok("inner_join()"); keeps only students who have a final GPA. That is an important limitation: the 37 students who left the programme have no final GPA, so the model can only predict the final GPA of students who stay. (Chapter 6 showed that the leavers were not a random group, so the model should not be used to judge them.)

The split, folds, and recipe follow Chapter 11. With a numeric outcome, #NormalTok("strata"); splits the outcome into quartiles and samples within each, so that both sets cover the full range of GPAs. The recipe adds #NormalTok("step_impute_mode()"); to fill in any missing categories:

