The best settings use trees of depth 1, and the best RMSE is 0.212. Trees of depth 1 use one predictor each, so a boosted model built from them adds up separate effects of each predictor, with no interactions. That the shallowest trees work best is another sign that the wellbeing data has no strong interactions for the trees to find.

