[#NormalTok("  Fitting Linear Mixed-Effects Models Using lme4. Journal of");],
[#NormalTok("  Statistical Software, 67(1), 1-48. doi:10.18637/jss.v067.i01.");],
[],
[#NormalTok("A BibTeX entry for LaTeX users is");],
[],
[#NormalTok("  @Article{,");],
[#NormalTok("    title = {Fitting Linear Mixed-Effects Models Using {lme4}},");],
[#NormalTok("    author = {Douglas Bates and Martin M{\\\"a}chler and Ben Bolker and Steve Walker},");],
[#NormalTok("    journal = {Journal of Statistical Software},");],
[#NormalTok("    year = {2015},");],
[#NormalTok("    volume = {67},");],
[#NormalTok("    number = {1},");],
[#NormalTok("    pages = {1--48},");],
[#NormalTok("    doi = {10.18637/jss.v067.i01},");],
[#NormalTok("  }");],));
]
]
A methods section might say: "Analyses were carried out in R version 4.4.3 \[R Core Team\], with mixed models fitted using lme4 version 1.1.37 \[Bates et al., 2015\]." Chapter 18 adds the question of disclosing the use of AI tools.

