The wrapper #NormalTok("I()"); lets a condition be used directly as the outcome, and #NormalTok("exponentiate = TRUE"); turns the log-odds into odds ratios and their confidence intervals.

#quote(block: true)[
Each one-point increase in stress (on the 1 to 5 scale) was associated with 3.6 times the odds of considering dropping out (95% CI 2.3 to 5.9), and each one-point increase in supervisor support with 0.33 times the odds (95% CI 0.22 to 0.49).
]

Chapters 11 to 15 went further with this question, asking how well dropout can be #emph[predicted]\; the thesis reports that logistic regression predicted as well as any machine learning model (a test AUC of about 0.84 in Chapter 11), which is itself a finding worth stating.

